## Aoi Tōdō Replaces Toji Fushiguro To Be The New Gym Inspiration For _JJK_ Fans
Introduced in the second season of [Gege Akutami’s](https://fandomwire.com/tag/gege-akutami/) _Jujutsu Kaisen,_ Fushiguro Toji was one of those broken characters who were blessed with superhuman strength, speed, and agility. Despite not having any cursed energy, he can not only inflict severe injury on jujutsu sorcerers but also kill them. Hence, he earned the title of ‘Sorcerer Killer.’

![Toji's physique was idolized by JJK fans](data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='1024'%20height='453'%20viewBox='0%200%201024%20453'%3E%3C/svg%3E)A still from Jujutsu Kaisen Season 2. Credits: MAPPA

While he was an assassin for hire, [Toji](https://fandomwire.com/he-broke-through-infinity-with-sheer-strength-the-biggest-jujutsu-kaisen-misconception-is-still-about-toji-and-gege-akatumi-is-partly-responsible-for-that/) became a gym inspiration for many fans, especially because of his broad shoulders and V-shaped torso, with well-defined arms, and rock-hard abs. Hence, that was enough for fans to make him their new idol.

[![Attack on Titan Cosplayer Has Abs So Defined Fans are Calling Her the Most “Lore Accurate Mikasa Ackerman”](data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='768'%20height='432'%20viewBox='0%200%20768%20432'%3E%3C/svg%3E)\
Related\
**Attack on Titan Cosplayer Has Abs So Defined Fans are Calling Her the Most “Lore Accurate Mikasa Ackerman”**](https://fandomwire.com/attack-on-titan-cosplayer-has-abs-so-defined-fans-are-calling-her-the-most-lore-accurate-mikasa-ackerman/)

However, it did not take long for the fans to realize that Aoi Tōdō was the man they should be worshipping. This is so because Tōdō’s build screams raw power and sheer physical dominance, with huge shoulders and an even bigger chest, with each muscle perfectly sculpted to precision.

![Toji has a sleeper build giving him unrivalled agility](data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='1024'%20height='455'%20viewBox='0%200%201024%20455'%3E%3C/svg%3E)Fushiguro Toji. Credits: MAPPA

Hence, he is the perfect example of a juggernaut present on the battlefield. One sheer difference between Aoi and Toji’s physique is that the latter’s build gives him unrivaled agility, but the former’s physique is sheer size and the very definition of a muscular build.

[![“Toei, pack it up”: Attack on Titan Director’s Promising Statement on The One Piece Remake Has Fans Convinced Eiichiro Oda’s Original Anime Will Get a Run for Its Money](data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20width='768'%20height='432'%20viewBox='0%200%20768%20432'%3E%3C/svg%3E)\
Related\
**“Toei, pack it up”: Attack on Titan Director’s Promising Statement on The One Piece Remake Has Fans Convinced Eiichiro Oda’s Original Anime Will Get a Run for Its Money**](https://fandomwire.com/toei-pack-it-up-attack-on-titan-directors-promising-statement-on-the-one-piece-remake-has-fans-convinced-eiichiro-odas-original-anime-will-get-a-run-for-its-money/)

Fans resonated with this notion as they shared a meme in [r/JuJutsuKaisen](https://www.reddit.com/r/JuJutsuKaisen/comments/1erv5wm/we_all_want_a_body_like_aoi/) with the caption, _“We all want a body like Aoi.”_ The post received an overwhelmingly positive reaction from fans, as they are in awe of his physique, which makes his presence known to his foes.

